I had some trouble again with NilFS yesterday, it's probably unrelated to my
last one which I never had the problem again. I started a rdiff-backup of my
/ to my backup server, went to sleep and when I woke up rdiff-backup was
stopped with a segfault and the computer wasn't responding, I switched
console and could login as root, it seems most processes using /home (where
NilFS is in use) were in D state. So I dumped as much information as I
could, sync'ed (sync Deadlocked too) and finally rebooted the hard way.

Here are the logs I gathered.

